																		Author Post
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="2303803"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1533528079 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Aug 2018 04:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3900099">
									

<p>It might be too bold. It's a Humes + meta + thaumaturgy triple-hit combo. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">But if you count the fact that I throw shade at Pataphysics in it, maybe that can deduct one and make it a two-hit combo.</span> But I'm gonna swing regardless.</p>
<p>Thank you to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thewydness" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3623441); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3623441&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533659880" alt="TheWydness" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3623441)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thewydness" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3623441); return false;">TheWydness</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sly161" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2969980); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2969980&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533659880" alt="Sly161" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2969980)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sly161" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2969980); return false;">Sly161</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varaxous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2433554); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2433554&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533659880" alt="Varaxous" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2433554)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varaxous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2433554); return false;">Varaxous</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/9volt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2800867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533659880" alt="9Volt" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2800867)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/9volt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;">9Volt</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/countless-skies" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3477314); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3477314&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533659880" alt="Countless Skies" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3477314)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/countless-skies" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3477314); return false;">Countless Skies</a></span> for feedback.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">why&nbsp;it's&nbsp;Series&nbsp;III</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Because</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The former 2758, called &quot;Self-Containment Processes&quot; (title changed to singular now), was a mess of an article IMO. It was +100 for being a really fancy format screw (it had .gif text 'n shit) and that's about it. It was super long and I just really Did Not Like It, from concept to execution all the way through.</p>
<p>Thus, this is taking the concept &#8212; &quot;self-containment&quot; &#8212; and completely running with it from there. The former one was not meta (it was an incorporeal hazard that affected humans) and did not involve a human as part of the anomaly.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Edit: There is no canon and all that, but I do want to make it clear that in my canon vision as the author, Pataphysics is not relevant here. All of those topics are covered under Multi-U in my eyes, and the explanation is what Wickerford says.</span> <sub>Okay after what <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-6807899/scp-2758#post-3902231">Bleep said here</a> idek so I'll leave it open to interpretation.</sub></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The very last expunged line said by Wardings says &quot;Several of your users — some of whom are rather prominent, as authors or moderators or otherwise — are in fact personnel from baseline reality assigned to monitor your site for legitimate information security threats and persons of interest.&quot; I ended up redacting it in the end because the &quot;other method of discouragement&quot; that Wardings mentions is the action of posting this document in our reality construct so that <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">you</span> we can read it and see what happened to this person, and the Foundation wouldn't want us to have that as a factual statement.</p>
<p><sub>Also, I do wanna make sure people get that the skip isn't the author. I'm not going to specify who it could be because it's a user that doesn't exist for us and is just for the sake of the narrative. The meta implication re: author is that I'm the Foundation agent who posted this. But no roleplaying on the forums.</sub></p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>

